# The corpus is gigabytes of fetched and generated fixtures and stays out; its Readme
# describes what is in it and is tracked, so a reader learns what the tests assume without
# having the corpus.
testdata/*
!testdata/Readme.md
.env.development
copilot-instructions.md
.context
context-*.md
*-context.md
# The root agent instructions are tracked; the same filenames deeper in the tree are not.
# A service's own AGENTS.md is its author's scratch and is free to cite the scratch folder,
# which the tracked tree forbids, so these rules stay unanchored and the root is negated.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.local.md
gain.ndjson
# Local scratch at any depth, wiped when the work it belongs to finishes. Nothing tracked
# may cite it, which is why it can be wiped safely.
plans/
hoover4.ini
# The real host detail — addresses, users, credentials, the network in front of the demo
# box. Deliberately at the top level so a scratch wipe cannot take it, and deliberately
# never tracked: docs/ and the skills are public.
INFRASTRUCTURE_INVENTORY.md
# Clones of the Liquid upstream repositories, worked on locally. They carry their own git
# history and their own remotes, so nothing under here is ever tracked by this repository.
external/
.serena/*
!.serena/project.yml

**/*.pyc
**/__pycache__
__pycache__
*.pyc